// Game: Postretro
// Format: Standard
// Teleporter acceptance fixture. All coordinates below are Quake map units.
// Spawn body center is 40 units above the floor, clearing the dev 1 metre capsule extreme.
// Floor markers: yellow = arm pad, red = arm button or closet plate, purple = classic gate (including returns), blue = disarm pad.
// Hub yellow use pad at minus 128 minus 128 arms the purple gate at minus 40 minus 184.
// Red plate at 64 0 disarms the gate and opens the two map-monster closet.
// Kill both closet residents. The authored death override removes them, then progress rearms the gate.
// Using the gate plays fixtures/jump and disarms it. The arrival is outside the seamless region.
// The purple lamp at minus 40 minus 232 tracks the gate: dim while disarmed, bright while armed.
// Room A center is 4096 0 and room B center is 8192 0. Landmark yaw delta is 90 degrees.
// Inside either room, cross the yellow pad to arm both seamless directions on the next tick.
// A peer outside the central region can use the red pad to shift an occupied room.
// Outer northeast use pads disarm the pair. Walk out of the central square and back in to return.
// Outer corner return regions lead back to the hub. Seamless routes carry no sound.
// The baseline removes only teleporter entities and destination points. Static geometry and lights match.
// Cheap bake defaults to one quarter metre per lightmap texel. No compiled output is committed.
